---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';

const path = '/alternatives/justuno-alternative';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'alternatives/justuno-alternative');
const desc = description(site, 'alternatives/justuno-alternative');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does Shopify listing availability mean Justuno shut down?",
    "answer": "No. The checked Pop-Ups & Spotlight listing says it is not currently available on the Shopify App Store and directs support questions to Justuno. Confirm the installation path and account status directly; the listing does not establish a company shutdown."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep Justuno while changing the sender?",
    "answer": "Consider that scope when the capture experience works. Verify the actual connector, destination fields and acceptance behavior with your chosen sender before enabling it."
  },
  {
    "question": "What must a quiz migration preserve?",
    "answer": "Keep the quiz version, answer meanings, result mapping, identity and permission provenance. Define whether omitted, blank and null fields preserve or clear an existing value, and test retries against duplicate enrollment."
  },
  {
    "question": "What happens to an incentive during handover?",
    "answer": "Carry the promised terms and eligibility into the receiving workflow. For an illustrative $208 order at 70% gross margin, fixed goods cost is $62.40; an 8% price discount reduces contribution from $145.60 to $128.96 before other costs."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 container">
    <a href="/alternatives" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All alternatives</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Justuno alternatives: retain capture or replace the handoff</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl text-slate-700">Evaluate the onsite form and quiz separately from the platform that sends the recovery message. A working capture experience may need a connector repair rather than replacement.</p>
    <div class="prose-shopify mt-10">
      <h2>Check installation scope before choosing a replacement</h2>
      <p>On November 25, 2026, Shopify's <a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/justuno-pop-ups-email-conversion">Pop-Ups &amp; Spotlight by Justuno listing</a> says the app is not currently available there and directs support questions to Justuno. This is a listing availability statement, not evidence of a company shutdown or the status of an existing installation. Ask Justuno which platform version, supported installation path and connector apply to your store before planning a reinstall.</p>
      <p>Justuno's <a class="link" href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/425-workflows-in-justuno">workflow documentation</a> describes onsite experiences and enrollment controls. Its <a class="link" href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/1054-visitor-id-resolution-identify">Visitor ID documentation</a> places abandonment follow-up in the connected ESP or CRM. A capture or identity feature does not by itself establish sending permission. Keep a working capture layer when its forms, quiz and destination handoff satisfy your requirements; fix a broken field mapping or destination rule before assuming the entire stack must move.</p>
      <h2>Preserve the quiz contract, not just the email address</h2>
      <p>Inventory published forms, quiz versions, result pages, display rules, hidden fields and incentive promises. Keep an explicit map from each answer code to its meaning and destination field. A renamed answer label can change segmentation even when the exported value looks unchanged. Preserve which version produced a result so a new recommendation model does not silently reinterpret old answers.</p>
      <p>For each destination, specify field types and update rules: omitted means no update, blank may mean an unanswered optional question, and null may be an intentional clear. Choose and demonstrate the actual behavior rather than assuming connectors agree. Protect an existing preference from an empty form submission, define precedence when checkout and a quiz disagree, and record the source and timestamp used to resolve it.</p>
      <h2>Identity and handoff acceptance</h2>
      <p>Keep capture submission ID, visitor ID where available, Shopify customer ID and destination profile ID separate. An email change, shared device or phone-only submission needs an explicit merge or review rule. Do not infer SMS permission from email permission or treat a matched identity as an opt-in. Carry the permission text/version, channel, purpose, source and withdrawal state to the sender.</p>
      <p>Document the exact connector scope: fields, list membership, events, update direction and whether a submission merely creates a profile or enrolls it. A successful outbound request is not proof the receiving workflow accepted the intended payload. Have the receiving operator verify stored values and the resulting enrollment. Keep a failed handoff visible for retry without generating another incentive or another recovery journey.</p>
      <h2>Proposed capture and recovery fixtures</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Submit an old quiz version and the current version for the same customer. Confirm answer meanings and result history survive; an omitted or null field must follow the agreed precedence rule.</li>
        <li>Retry the same submission after a connector timeout. Use a stable submission key to prevent duplicate enrollment or coupon issuance, then verify acceptance at the destination.</li>
        <li>Restore a cart after mobile distraction, and after a financing interruption. Check that the destination can identify the current cart and provide the relevant help without treating a profile creation as a purchase.</li>
        <li>For shipping shock, gift sizing and an unavailable variant, preserve the quiz result while validating current delivery and stock facts. A recommendation must not advertise an unavailable item.</li>
        <li>For a minimum-order block, stacked coupon or repeat purchaser, verify the promised incentive's eligibility, exclusions and minimum spend before the sender repeats it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These are acceptance proposals, not observed merchant results. Include a purchase and a withdrawal between capture and send, a delayed event and a duplicate identity. Check suppression in the sending platform using current state. Record an uncertain identity or failed destination acceptance as held work, rather than guessing that a message should be sent.</p>
      <h2>Keep the incentive economically consistent</h2>
      <p>For an illustrative $208 order at 70% gross margin, goods cost remains $62.40. Full-price contribution is $145.60; an 8% selling-price discount leaves $191.36 revenue and $128.96 contribution, a $16.64 reduction before other variable costs. Include payment fees, shipping support, returns, capture software and sending costs when comparing total contribution. Attributed revenue is not incremental lift; use enough data for a meaningful comparison cohort where feasible.</p>
      <p>If an onsite form promises a code, carry its actual terms and redemption state to the sender. A handoff retry must not create a second offer, extend an expiry silently or erase a previous redemption. Retain capture when repairing this boundary is enough. Replace the form or quiz when its required experience cannot be demonstrated, and replace the sender only for a demonstrated sending requirement.</p>
      <h2>Evaluate candidates at the right boundary</h2>
      <p>For capture replacement, start with a field-by-field and quiz-result demonstration; <a class="link" href="/alternatives/privy-alternative">Privy's evaluation guide</a> provides a related capture decision. For a sender change, compare <a class="link" href="/alternatives/klaviyo-alternative">Klaviyo</a> and <a class="link" href="/alternatives/omnisend-alternative">Omnisend</a> against your destination acceptance fixtures. <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy</a> may be worth evaluating for a simpler lifecycle workflow if it demonstrates the required handoff; no direct Justuno connector or quiz parity is assumed. An SMS-only evaluation through <a class="link" href="/alternatives/postscript-alternative">Postscript</a> or <a class="link" href="/alternatives/recart-alternative">Recart</a> still needs its own permission and queue checks.</p>
      <h2>Cut over one owner, with a replay ledger</h2>
      <p>Inventory capture callers and existing welcome, cart and SMS queues. Stop new enrollment on the outgoing path and choose which pending work drains or is canceled. Give each cart/channel one sending owner. Retain submission and event identifiers, destination acceptance records, actual sends and current suppressions so replay cannot restart completed work. Roll back by pausing the new path, reconciling purchases, withdrawals and messages already sent, then resuming only eligible work in the retained system. Readiness comes from accepted fixtures and measurement, not a promised number of days.</p>
    </div>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="FAQ: Justuno alternatives" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
